<title>JAPAN: Japan car shares steered higher by weaker yen.</title>
<headline>Japan car shares steered higher by weaker yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese car shares cruised higher in Wednesday morning trade due to the weaker yen, brokers said.</p>
<p>The yen fell overnight to around the 114 yen to the dollar level.</p>
<p>As of 0051 GMT, Honda Motor Co Ltd shares were 50 yen higher at 2,740 yen. Toyota Motor Corp added 20 yen to reach 2,750, making it the 15th most heavily traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange.</p>
</text>
